Section 11. Valid Causes for Separation. - The following are valid causes for
separation pursuant to a bona fide reorganization:


a. A position has been abolished or rendered redundant;


b. Positions are merged, divided, or consolidated to meet the exigencies

of the service;

c. Causes allowed by the Civil Service Law.

An online system that can easily and readily record and provide accurate and reliable government human resources data. The inventory covers HR in the career and non-career service of the government including those appointed by the President.

The following modules shall comprise the IGHR system:

A. Online Agency/HR Profile Management System – HR data submission of agency profiling and tracking

and monitoring of agency HR systems/programs;
B. Inventory module – individual and consolidated agency inventory/statistical reports;
C. Plantilla module – agency plantilla of positions, including career and non-career status;
D. electronic Personal Data Sheet – retrieval, recording and updating of employees PDS data;
E. Service Card – Employment history of individual government employees
F. CS Job Portal - online listing on vacant position in government offices open for applicants;
G. SALN Digitization – corresponding SALN of government employees shall be linked to their PDS data;
H. PRIME-HRM - It is a mechanism that assesses and accredits the maturity level of government agencies

